To solve the equation $3(r-5)=24$, first expand the term on the left side, then isolate the variable.\\
\( 3(r-5)=24 \) \\
\( \Rightarrow\qquad 3r - 15 = 24 \) \\
\( \Rightarrow\qquad 3r = 24 + 15 \) \\
\( \Rightarrow\qquad 3r = 39 \) \\
\( \Rightarrow\qquad r = \frac{39}{3} \)

Basis for answer choice elimination: Multiplying or dividing any value of the variable $r$ by $3$ changes its value. Thus, the answer choice must be a multiple of $3$.\\

